# Xbox Wireless Controller / Elite Series 2 over Bluetooth (045e:0b22, bus 0005).
#
# The Bluetooth HID descriptor includes a keyboard collection for the Xbox and
# Share buttons, so udev's input_id classifier tags the pad ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD
# and never sets ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK. SDL2's udev backend enumerates only devices
# carrying that tag, so EmulationStation and RetroArch cannot see the pad at all
# - while the kernel is delivering perfectly good BTN_GAMEPAD/EV_ABS events.
# Over USB the descriptor is clean, it is classified correctly, and it works;
# hence "only works when plugged in".
#
# Scoped to this exact bustype/vendor/product so nothing else is affected.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", \
  ATTRS{id/bustype}=="0005", ATTRS{id/vendor}=="045e", ATTRS{id/product}=="0b22", \
  ENV{ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK}="1"
